WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.679
Now let's introduce coalesce Coalesce returns the
first value in

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:09.637
a list that is not null For example we might try an

00:00:09.662 --> 00:00:15.023
email address first If that is missing try the
mobile phone If

00:00:15.049 --> 00:00:19.546
that is also missing try the home phone Finally we
can return

00:00:19.572 --> 00:00:24.160
a readable fallback This is a very useful function
but we should

00:00:24.186 --> 00:00:29.095
use it carefully A fallback should have a real
meaning We do

00:00:29.121 --> 00:00:32.137
not want to replace missing data with a value that
changes the

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:36.583
meaning of the information In a few slides we will
combine coalesce

00:00:36.608 --> 00:00:39.456
with null if so that blank text is treated as
missing before

00:00:39.469 --> 00:00:41.711
we choose the first usable contact method
